{
  "id": "Compound::DB01189 - Gene::2554",
  "verbalization": "Desflurane is implicated in the interaction with Gaba receptor activity through its binding to Gabrq, Gabrb1, or Gabrg3, all of which are subunits of the Gaba-a receptor. These receptors are ultimately associated with Gabra1, suggesting a potential role for Desflurane in modulating Gaba-a receptor function. The evidence indicates that Desflurane may influence Gabra1 through a shared pathway involving Gaba receptor activity, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The consistent involvement of Gaba receptor activity as a mediator across different binding sites suggests a broader role for Desflurane in regulating Gaba signaling, potentially through a common downstream effect on Gabra1. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Gaba receptors in the pharmacological effects of Desflurane, though further studies are needed to elucidate the precise molecular interactions.",
